As quoted from <42299@ut-emx.uucp> by moxley@ccwf.cc.utexas.edu (Richard Moxley):
+---------------
| Does anyone (dev. team maybe) know if save files can be ported from one
| implementation of NetHack to another?  I'm interested in going from several
| save files created under MS-DOS NetHack to Macintosh NetHack.  I think
| they are the same version.
+---------------

680x0 processors (Mac, Amiga) have a different byte ordering from 80x86
processors (MS-DOS and 386/486 UNIX).  Neither can read the other, although if
you knew the format of the save file you might be able to write a program to
selectively swap bytes.  ("Selectively" because you don't want to swap bytes
in strings, for example.)

